        answer: 3,
        explanation: "The first six terms are $2,\\;4,\\;8,\\;16,\\;32,\\;64.$ Alternatively, use the geometric sequence formula. $a_n=a_1r^{n-1}$ $a_6=2(2)^5$ $a_6=64$",
